{
  "repo": "vedprakash-m/tenet-copilot",
  "number": 28,
  "title": "Rename project to Tenet Copilot",
  "body": "## Outcome and evidence\n\nRenames the public project and repository identity to Tenet Copilot while preserving `/tenet`, `/tenet-review`, `.tenet/`, `tenet.policy.json`, `kernel/tenet.mjs`, `TENET_*`, `Tenet-Work`, and `tenet/` branch naming. Updates package/plugin identity, repository URLs, release artifact naming with a legacy migration alias, canonical specs, user docs, and release verification. Also includes the authorized production-readiness fixes for call-boundary recovery, storage, starter restore safety, CI determinism, and hosted performance.\n\nPrivacy/range scans are clean. Hosted `Tenet validation` passed on the exact functional head, including all source shards, Windows lanes, bundled payloads and all UAT groups. The independent `System budgets` job remains failed only on the long-history warm-latency row; the 300 ms budget has not been weakened or skipped.\n\n## Compatibility and release notes\n\n- [x] Classified as a pre-1.0 minor compatibility change; runtime commands and state contracts remain stable.\n- [x] Kernel/plugin SemVer agree at `0.2.0-m0`.\n- [x] Release disclosures cover changed repository/package/plugin identity, executable and destination naming, migration alias, support text, and unchanged permissions/schemas/evaluators.\n\n## Maintainer review (ENG-07, ENG-11)\n\n- [x] Consequential changes were reviewed immediately; findings were fixed or disclosed.\n- [x] External reviewer was requested when available. Agent review does not count as second-maintainer review.\n- [x] Review disclosure is complete; no second maintainer was available.\n- [x] Owner-approved amendment removes calendar waiting from ENG-11. Merge may occur when required checks and review disclosure are complete.\n\nExternal reviewer or unavailable: unavailable; owner is the sole maintainer.\n\nThe owner merges; this PR does not authorize publication or bypass release gates.",
